OPTION 1: AGPL-3.0-only WITH SCE Linking Exception
================================================================================

Use this for:
- Open source projects compatible with AGPL-3.0
- Applications, including closed-source commercial ones, that use the
  UNMODIFIED engine (static or dynamic linking). The Linking Exception
  keeps AGPL-3.0 off your application and waives the source offer.
- State machine code generated by an UNMODIFIED sce-codegen, used in
  your application (Linking Exception, section 3)

The Linking Exception does NOT apply to:
- A MODIFIED engine or generator. It is governed by AGPL-3.0 in full,
  including the network clause (section 13): users who interact with it
  over a network are entitled to its source.
- A competing product: an SDK, library, framework, runtime, development
  tool or hosted service that offers state-machine execution, SCXML
  processing, code generation or authoring to others. It is governed by
  AGPL-3.0 in full.

